<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p><m>P = {\left[\begin{array}{cc} -2 &amp; -3 \\ -3 &amp; -1 \end{array}\right]}</m> and <m>Q = {\left[\begin{array}{cc} -1 &amp; -3 \\ 0 &amp; -1 \end{array}\right]}</m>. A shape is transformed by <m>P</m>, and its image is then transformed by <m>Q</m>.</p><p>(a) Find the single matrix that maps the shape straight onto its final image.</p><div><fillin characters="3" name="ans1"/>  </div><p>(b) <m>K({3},\,{-2})</m> is a vertex of the shape. Find its final image.</p><div>( <fillin characters="5" name="ans2"/> , <fillin characters="5" name="ans3"/> )   </div></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>The matrix of the transformation done first is written on the right, next to the point it acts on. <m>P</m> is done first, so the single matrix is <m>QP</m>:</p><p><m>QP = {\left[\begin{array}{cc} -1 &amp; -3 \\ 0 &amp; -1 \end{array}\right]}{\left[\begin{array}{cc} -2 &amp; -3 \\ -3 &amp; -1 \end{array}\right]} = {\left[\begin{array}{cc} 11 &amp; 6 \\ 3 &amp; 1 \end{array}\right]}</m></p><p>(b) <m>{\left[\begin{array}{cc} 11 &amp; 6 \\ 3 &amp; 1 \end{array}\right]}{\left[\begin{array}{c} 3 \\ -2 \end{array}\right]} = {\left[\begin{array}{c} 21 \\ 7 \end{array}\right]}</m>, so the final image of K is <m>({21},\,{7})</m>. Check in two steps: <m>P</m> sends K to <m>({0},\,{-7})</m>, and <m>Q</m> sends that point to <m>({21},\,{7})</m>.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>\left[\begin{array}{cc} 11 &amp; 6 \\ 3 &amp; 1 \end{array}\right]</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>21</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>7</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>